<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.AFRICAN SEPT GOLD/FOREX RESERVES 10.04 BLN RAND.</title>
<headline>S.AFRICAN SEPT GOLD/FOREX RESERVES 10.04 BLN RAND.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's combined gold and</p>
<p>foreign exchange reserves fell 35.68 million rand in September</p>
<p>to 10.04 billion rand from August's 10.08 billion rand, when</p>
<p>they fell 292.1 million rand, Reserve Bank figures show.</p>
<p>Economists polled by Reuters had forecast September reserves</p>
<p>at 10.06 billion rand, with the range 9.8 to 10.5 billion rand.</p>
<p>  Details(rounded)    Sept '96	    Aug '96     Sept '95</p>
<p>Assets: (Rand millions)</p>
<p>  Gold		    5991.14	     6264.30     5727.34 </p>
<p>  Foreign		 4051.39	     3813.92     6065.22</p>
<p>  Total		  10042.54	    10078.22    11792.55</p>
<p>  Gold shr of total     59.7   pct	  62.2	  48.57</p>
<p>  Gold volume		3.86  mln oz	3.99	  4.55</p>
<p>  Gold value	    1550.46  rand/oz  1567.26     1258.52</p>
<p>  Other liabilities	6.17  bln rand    5.49	  5.90</p>
<p>  Total liabilities     32.86  bln rand   31.42	 32.98</p>
<p>NOTE: The Reserve Bank said that foreign credit lines</p>
<p>amounting to 612 million rand were utilised over the month-end.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom (+27 11 482-1003)</p>
</text>
